WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:00.020
{ED}

00:03.000 --> 00:04.650
You see it?

00:04.650 --> 00:07.610
Mighty fine day here today.

00:07.610 --> 00:09.860
Oh, that looks great!

00:09.860 --> 00:11.820
The waters are so calm!

00:12.620 --> 00:16.210
Tokyo's in full-on rainy season mode.

00:16.770 --> 00:18.670
<i>Guess what, Mitsumi-chan?</i>

00:18.670 --> 00:19.740
Hmm?

00:19.740 --> 00:22.540
<i>There's a guy I like.</i>

00:25.930 --> 00:27.200
<i>You okay?</i>

00:27.200 --> 00:28.500
R-Really?!

02:10.260 --> 02:12.420
<i>Fumi's in love, huh?</i>

02:13.380 --> 02:15.170
<i>I feel left behind.</i>

02:15.730 --> 02:20.640
<i>But that makes sense. We </i>are<i> at that age now.</i>

02:20.640 --> 02:24.350
<i>He's in a different class, 
but we're both in the tennis club.</i>

02:24.350 --> 02:26.580
<i>He's a real funny one.</i>

02:26.580 --> 02:29.000
Huh? Ohh...

02:29.000 --> 02:31.460
<i>F-Fumi, can I ask you something?</i>

02:31.460 --> 02:32.250
Hmm?

02:32.250 --> 02:38.030
Uh, how... what's it like? Love, I mean.

02:38.030 --> 02:39.510
<i>Well, for me...</i>

02:39.940 --> 02:44.110
First, I thought, 
"This guy's fun! I like him!"

02:44.110 --> 02:47.170
Before I knew it, my eyes kept following him.

02:47.170 --> 02:52.060
Soon, I got excited about school, 
cause I knew I'd see him there!

02:52.060 --> 02:56.110
Then I started hanging in his class, 
acting like I was there to see friends.

02:56.110 --> 03:00.230
Squee! It feels so weird 
talking to you about this stuff!

03:00.230 --> 03:03.910
But then I'd get super nervous 
whenever I'd get to talk to him.

03:03.910 --> 03:07.530
<i>I'd keep worrying about 
the right things to say,</i>

03:07.530 --> 03:09.310
<i>keep wanting to
run away mid-sentence...</i>

03:09.310 --> 03:11.420
<i>It's exciting, but it's  
doing a number on me!</i>

03:14.310 --> 03:16.560
<i>You want to see someone, 
but you also run from them.</i>

03:16.560 --> 03:19.280
<i>You want to talk to them, 
but you trip over your words...</i>

03:19.280 --> 03:21.540
<i>How complicated.</i>

03:21.540 --> 03:24.340
<i>Assuming I fall in love someday,</i>

03:24.340 --> 03:27.680
<i>will I be able to recognize it?</i>

03:28.440 --> 03:31.280
<i>I should ask Makocchan and 
Yuzu-chan when I get to class.</i>

03:31.280 --> 03:33.970
Oh yeah, they'll be handing 
'em out today, right?

03:33.970 --> 03:35.650
We're exactly two weeks away and all.

03:35.650 --> 03:38.350
What, seriously? Seriously!

03:38.350 --> 03:40.690
Yikes, I thought we had more time!

03:40.690 --> 03:43.320
<i>That's right! I don't have time 
to think about love!</i>

03:43.320 --> 03:46.330
<i>Today's the day it gets announced!</i>

03:46.330 --> 03:49.080
<b>Term Final Exam Syllabus</b>

03:49.080 --> 03:51.260
You probably know the drill 
after middle school,

03:51.260 --> 03:54.000
but club activities will be suspended 
throughout the exam period.

03:54.660 --> 03:57.520
You'll also be prohibited from 
entering the faculty office.

03:57.520 --> 04:00.210
If you have any questions, 
ask for us and wait outside.

04:00.680 --> 04:05.220
Do your best, and close out the first half 
of your first year with a smile!

04:05.220 --> 04:07.380
Okay, let's take attendance.

04:06.100 --> 04:08.530
<i>The day has come.</i>

04:07.410 --> 04:08.530
Asano-san?

04:08.530 --> 04:09.410
Here.

04:09.410 --> 04:10.550
Iwakura-san?

04:10.550 --> 04:11.470
Here.

04:11.470 --> 04:14.750
<i>In the midterms, I upped my 
rank to ninth in my year.</i>

04:14.750 --> 04:16.330
<i>I'm surrounded by excellent students,</i>

04:16.330 --> 04:19.950
<i>so I know it's not good to be 
obsessed with the ranking,</i>

04:19.950 --> 04:23.760
<i>but given I'm aiming for Tokyo U, I need 
to stay comfortably in the single digits.</i>

04:23.760 --> 04:27.980
Shima-kun... called in sick today.

04:27.980 --> 04:29.140
Jougasaki-san?

04:29.140 --> 04:30.010
Here.

04:30.010 --> 04:31.080
Suda-kun?

04:31.080 --> 04:31.680
Here.

04:31.630 --> 04:34.380
<i>So Shima-kun's out today...</i>

04:31.680 --> 04:32.810
Soga-kun?

04:32.810 --> 04:33.560
Here.

04:33.560 --> 04:34.380
Takato-kun?

04:34.380 --> 04:35.000
Here.

04:36.750 --> 04:39.140
Didn't we <i>just</i> have exams?

04:39.140 --> 04:43.160
It includes material from midterms, 
so that's a lot of pages.

04:43.160 --> 04:46.640
How are we already through the first 
half of the year? That is scary.

04:46.640 --> 04:49.850
God, where do I even begin?

04:50.290 --> 04:53.580
Look at Mitsumi. She looks 
like she was born ready.

04:54.370 --> 04:58.080
Well, I <i>am</i> looking to graduate Tokyo U's 
law school and join the government.

04:58.080 --> 04:59.650
Exams are nothing!

04:59.650 --> 05:01.830
Irritating, but a good role model.

05:01.830 --> 05:04.070
Teach me, Mitsumi-sensei!

05:04.070 --> 05:07.630
What awful timing for Shima-kun 
to get sick. I feel bad for him.

05:07.630 --> 05:08.460
Right?

05:08.460 --> 05:09.900
Maybe I should text him.

05:09.900 --> 05:12.990
He might want to know the exam syllabus ASAP.

05:13.830 --> 05:16.580
<i>Yeah, but we're two weeks away.</i>

05:16.580 --> 05:19.840
<i>That'd be the last thing 
I'd want to see if I was sick.</i>

05:19.840 --> 05:27.340
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

05:19.840 --> 05:27.340
<b>Today</b>

05:19.840 --> 05:27.340
<b>Good morning, Shima-kun.
Sensei said you were out sick.
Are you okay? It's such an
important time, too. That sucks!
The final exam syllabus gets
announced today, so if you
want to know, I'll tell you.
It'll include material from
midterms, so I'm sure it'll be
a lot... I'll show you the notes
I take while you're out sick,
so don't worry about that!
Just focus on resting well
and taking care of yourself.
Get well soon.</b>

05:20.090 --> 05:27.340
<b>Morning</b>

05:20.570 --> 05:21.400
Oh.

05:21.130 --> 05:27.340
<b>Was asleep</b>

05:21.890 --> 05:24.030
He replied quickly, so he can't be that sick.

05:24.030 --> 05:25.500
That's a relief.

05:25.260 --> 05:27.340
<b>I woke up so late, I was just, like,
whatever. So don't worry, I'm fine.
Thanks, though!</b>

05:28.710 --> 05:32.940
Huh? But Sensei said he called in sick.

05:32.940 --> 05:35.350
Probably just called and went back to sleep.

05:35.350 --> 05:37.090
But that's skipping!

05:37.090 --> 05:38.150
Sure is.

05:38.150 --> 05:42.190
What? He doesn't hate school, does he?

05:42.190 --> 05:43.570
Nah.

05:43.570 --> 05:46.450
Sousuke was like that even in middle school.

05:47.140 --> 05:49.930
He wouldn't cancel plans with people,

05:49.930 --> 05:54.630
but he'd sometimes silently skip stuff 
if it wouldn't bother anybody.

05:55.910 --> 06:00.080
<i>Come to think of it, he was late 
for the entrance ceremony, too.</i>

06:00.080 --> 06:01.800
It's just the entrance ceremony.

06:02.960 --> 06:04.170
Forget that!

06:04.170 --> 06:06.170
You went to the same middle school, right?

06:06.170 --> 06:10.620
Is it true that one in every 
three girls asked him out?!

06:10.620 --> 06:13.200
And that he tore them up and tossed them?! {they're talking about the letters, she's thinking martial arts}

06:11.800 --> 06:14.350
<b></b>Tossed them?

06:13.200 --> 06:16.250
I hear he enjoyed the nightlife, 
even at that age!

06:15.470 --> 06:17.430
<b></b>Lord of the Night?

06:16.250 --> 06:18.900
Well, I heard he was dating 
a magazine model from another school

06:18.600 --> 06:21.610
<b></b>Magazine model?

06:18.900 --> 06:21.610
and wouldn't give any other 
girls the time of day.

06:21.610 --> 06:22.880
Is any of this true?

06:22.880 --> 06:24.270
I don't know!

06:24.270 --> 06:26.770
And don't ask me things 
you wouldn't ask him!

06:27.360 --> 06:30.130
Mukai-kun's got a good 
head on his shoulders...

06:30.130 --> 06:31.660
Look at Mr. Popular over here.

06:32.590 --> 06:34.660
<i>Is Shima-kun actually...</i>

06:35.300 --> 06:36.330
<i>a bad boy?!</i>

06:37.160 --> 06:39.060
<i>No, stop that.</i>

06:39.060 --> 06:42.520
<i>Didn't I tell myself I wouldn't 
take these things at face value?</i>

06:47.340 --> 06:49.160
Sh... Shima-kun?!

06:48.550 --> 06:50.180
<b>Conquer the Nation</b>

06:49.220 --> 06:52.390
<b>Rice</b>

06:49.220 --> 06:52.390
<b>Love and Energy</b>

06:50.140 --> 06:52.390
Waddup, Mitsumi-chan!

06:52.390 --> 06:54.370
What's gotten into you?

06:54.370 --> 06:57.010
It's almost July! Aren't you hot?

06:57.010 --> 06:59.680
Nah. I feel the wind on my trusty steed.

06:59.680 --> 07:01.030
Perfect timing, though.

07:01.030 --> 07:03.150
Give this to the teachers for me.

07:04.900 --> 07:07.650
<b>Drop Out Notice</b>

07:05.210 --> 07:07.650
B-But why?

07:08.020 --> 07:09.920
Is something bothering you?

07:09.920 --> 07:12.080
Nah, just not feeling it.

07:12.080 --> 07:14.070
Like, who cares, you know?

07:17.050 --> 07:19.080
Adios!

07:20.310 --> 07:23.360
Shima-kun!

07:30.840 --> 07:32.970
<i>What an awful dream.</i>

07:33.660 --> 07:34.850
Satou-san?

07:34.850 --> 07:35.970
Here.

07:36.430 --> 07:37.970
Shima-kun?

07:37.970 --> 07:41.370
Huh? But he didn't call in today.

07:41.850 --> 07:43.850
Did anyone hear anything?

07:45.240 --> 07:48.110
<i>Again? Is he okay?</i>

07:48.780 --> 07:51.010
<i>I mean, taking two days off 
just for oversleeping?</i>

07:51.010 --> 07:53.560
<i>Is he actually sick?</i>

07:54.280 --> 07:56.560
<i>Or in some kind of trouble?</i>

07:57.940 --> 08:00.620
<i>He doesn't seem like 
the type to talk about it...</i>

08:04.780 --> 08:08.060
<i>What if he really stops coming to school?</i>

08:10.670 --> 08:11.950
Morning.

08:11.950 --> 08:13.010
"Morning"?

08:13.010 --> 08:14.510
It's lunchtime, man!

08:14.510 --> 08:16.930
The low-pressure system gave me a headache.

08:16.930 --> 08:19.750
I feel you. I'm so sleepy too.

08:19.750 --> 08:22.050
But two days in a row? Come on, dude.

08:22.050 --> 08:24.200
Hey, I'm here now, aren't I?

08:24.200 --> 08:26.520
Oh, morning, Mitsumi-chan.

08:35.070 --> 08:37.360
Okay, let's call it a day here.

08:37.360 --> 08:38.200
Stand!

08:39.470 --> 08:40.700
Bow!

08:40.700 --> 08:42.370
Wanna study together?

08:42.370 --> 08:43.210
Sure!

08:43.210 --> 08:44.570
Where, though?

08:44.570 --> 08:46.700
Gotta be a diner, right?

08:45.080 --> 08:48.000
Oh, class officers. Please stay back.

08:48.000 --> 08:51.760
Could you staple these printouts 
together for tomorrow?

08:51.760 --> 08:52.730
Sure.

08:53.130 --> 08:53.760
Okay.

08:54.670 --> 08:56.880
<i>Why'd it have to be today?</i>

09:12.990 --> 09:16.400
Uh, Mitsumi-chan? Are you 
mad at me or something?

09:16.980 --> 09:20.530
I'm not... <i>mad</i>, but...

09:20.530 --> 09:21.580
But?

09:22.810 --> 09:26.530
Did you really skip school 
just because you were sleepy?

09:26.530 --> 09:28.320
Huh? Yeah.

09:28.320 --> 09:30.280
The rainy season sucks for me.

09:30.280 --> 09:33.580
You'll miss out on important 
announcements during exam season.

09:33.580 --> 09:35.420
I guess.

09:35.420 --> 09:38.050
Well, all I really care about is passing.

09:39.160 --> 09:41.190
Was that all?

09:41.190 --> 09:42.760
Like, who cares, you know?

09:44.770 --> 09:46.890
<b>Drop Out Notice</b>

09:47.200 --> 09:48.940
I... I care!

09:48.940 --> 09:50.200
What's gotten into you?

09:50.200 --> 09:52.940
A-And you should care more about 
yourself and your reputation!

09:52.940 --> 09:56.050
People will keep saying you're out 
enjoying the nightlife and stuff!

09:58.070 --> 09:59.530
Did someone tell you that?

10:06.140 --> 10:08.380
Well, I just heard it in passing yesterday.

10:08.380 --> 10:10.750
Anyway, all I'm trying to say is,

10:10.750 --> 10:13.180
term finals are important 
even for first-years...

10:13.180 --> 10:16.190
Maybe they are to you.

10:29.860 --> 10:30.800
Sorry!

10:35.460 --> 10:39.220
There, all done! I'll take these 
to the faculty office!

10:39.220 --> 10:40.060
No, let me—

10:40.060 --> 10:42.820
It's fine! I had a question 
for Sensei, anyway!

10:42.820 --> 10:44.670
See you tomorrow!

10:44.670 --> 10:45.510
Mits—

10:58.970 --> 11:02.970
<u>Scene 06: Drizzling and Flickering</u>

11:06.630 --> 11:09.100
Maybe that's all it is to you!

11:12.390 --> 11:15.360
Maybe they are to you.

11:19.500 --> 11:22.610
<i>He was holding a grudge!</i>

11:23.150 --> 11:26.080
<i>I stepped way over the line!</i>

11:26.080 --> 11:28.370
<i>Yeah, I mean, Shima-kun's the kind of guy</i>

11:28.370 --> 11:32.370
<i>who tends to take a step back 
in group settings and listen in.</i>

11:32.370 --> 11:37.750
<i>He must hate people prying into his life, 
like with the child actor thing.</i>

11:38.100 --> 11:40.010
<i>But wait! Let's go over this!</i>

11:40.010 --> 11:42.900
<i>Maybe that's all it is to you!</i>

11:41.050 --> 11:43.010
<b>Entrance Ceremony</b>

11:42.900 --> 11:44.040
<i>The similarity...</i>

11:43.010 --> 11:44.050
<b>Entrance Ceremony</b>

11:44.040 --> 11:47.010
Maybe they are to you.

11:44.050 --> 11:49.270
<b>Entrance Ceremony</b>

11:44.180 --> 11:49.270
<b>Late June</b>

11:47.010 --> 11:49.270
<b>More Than
2 Months Later!</b>

11:47.010 --> 11:49.270
<i>...doesn't mean it was intentional, right?</i>

11:49.270 --> 11:52.460
<i>Maybe I'm just giving what I said 
too much importance!</i>

11:52.460 --> 11:53.920
<i>Maybe it was just a coincidence!</i>

11:53.920 --> 11:55.770
<i>Come to think of it, his tone was different!</i>

11:55.770 --> 11:58.870
Maybe they are to you.

11:59.240 --> 12:01.160
Different strokes 
for different folks, right?

12:01.940 --> 12:05.110
<i>Yeah, I'm starting to think 
that's what he meant.</i>

12:05.110 --> 12:07.180
<i>He probably wasn't mad at all.</i>

12:07.180 --> 12:10.480
<i>I was just jumping to the
worst possible conclusion.</i>

12:10.480 --> 12:12.650
<i>Either way, I'll find out tomorrow,</i>

12:12.650 --> 12:15.570
<i>so I should focus on studying for now.</i>

12:15.570 --> 12:17.130
<i>Focus, focus...</i>

12:25.690 --> 12:28.310
Was I holding a grudge over it?

12:28.730 --> 12:30.340
What, you looking for advice?

12:30.340 --> 12:31.930
At this hour?

12:31.930 --> 12:34.190
Seriously, Sousuke, 
when are you gonna go home?

12:34.190 --> 12:37.030
Mind hearing me out, Chris-kun?

12:37.030 --> 12:39.210
Uh, I'm trying to study.

12:39.210 --> 12:41.440
Aren't your term finals soon, too?

12:41.440 --> 12:44.120
There's this girl. 
We're class officers together.

12:44.120 --> 12:44.920
Huh?

12:45.690 --> 12:48.240
<i>You</i>? A class officer?

12:49.220 --> 12:50.770
Yeah, forget it. I should go.

12:50.770 --> 12:53.130
Sorry, sorry. So what about this girl?

12:53.130 --> 12:55.310
She's really straight-laced.

12:55.310 --> 12:59.690
She couldn't believe that 
I skipped school for a silly reason.

12:59.690 --> 13:02.460
She yelled at me, saying it wasn't good.

13:00.000 --> 13:02.460
<b>The Class Rep</b>

13:00.750 --> 13:02.460
<b>Type</b>

13:02.990 --> 13:08.260
So I kinda snapped back at her 
in a passive-aggressive tone.

13:08.790 --> 13:10.720
It probably hurt her.

13:10.720 --> 13:14.580
Yikes. You need to cut that out.

13:14.580 --> 13:17.960
It makes it seem like behind that smile, 
you're mad as all hell. It's scary!

13:17.960 --> 13:20.530
But isn't that unusual for you?

13:20.530 --> 13:21.480
Huh?

13:21.480 --> 13:25.190
It's always in one ear 
and out the other with you.

13:25.190 --> 13:27.980
Oh... Yeah, it's weird.

13:27.980 --> 13:30.330
She's the best friend I have among the girls.

13:30.330 --> 13:33.490
So I guess I just didn't 
wanna hear it from her.

13:33.490 --> 13:34.720
My!

13:34.720 --> 13:38.700
You should really tell her that!

13:39.440 --> 13:41.490
Nah, I'll pass.

13:41.490 --> 13:47.420
Like, I don't really see the point 
of "clearing the air" kinda talks.

13:47.420 --> 13:50.750
If things are fine, 
they'll stay fine either way.

13:50.750 --> 13:53.350
And if they're not, no amount 
of talking will make them fine.

13:53.350 --> 13:55.420
<i>Talk about detached.</i>

13:55.990 --> 13:57.140
<i>But...</i>

13:57.140 --> 13:59.180
Okay, time to bounce.

13:59.180 --> 13:59.960
Bye.

13:59.960 --> 14:06.280
<i>The fact that you're talking about any 
kind of relationship is headline news.</i>

14:12.440 --> 14:15.340
<i>I couldn't focus at all.</i>

14:15.910 --> 14:19.130
<i>A-Anyway, I'll go to class,</i>

14:19.130 --> 14:21.540
<i>and if Shima-kun's there, 
I'll say good morning to him.</i>

14:22.330 --> 14:23.750
<i>With a bright smile!</i>

14:23.750 --> 14:26.050
<i>Like I'm not bothered by anything!</i>

14:26.360 --> 14:27.220
Oh.

14:29.970 --> 14:31.050
Morning.

14:31.050 --> 14:33.810
<b>Bloodshot eyes</b>

14:31.550 --> 14:33.810
<b>Frizzy hair due
to the humidity</b>

14:32.050 --> 14:33.810
<b>The not-smile
she wasn't
ready to give</b>

14:32.550 --> 14:33.810
<b>Low, strangled voice</b>

14:35.810 --> 14:36.990
Morning.

14:37.890 --> 14:39.660
<i>She's mad as hell!</i>

14:51.230 --> 14:52.780
Suddenly got cold today, huh?

14:53.240 --> 14:55.100
Y-Yeah!

14:56.630 --> 14:59.410
It's more than ten degrees 
colder than yesterday.

14:59.410 --> 15:01.490
It's that rainy season chill.

15:01.490 --> 15:02.590
Sure is.

15:09.220 --> 15:13.050
<b>Fin</b>

15:10.450 --> 15:12.400
<i>We talked about the weather, and that was it.</i>

15:13.050 --> 15:14.280
Yo, 'sup!

15:14.280 --> 15:15.500
Morning.

15:17.560 --> 15:18.490
Morning.

15:18.490 --> 15:19.720
Morning, Shima-kun.

15:19.720 --> 15:20.720
Morning.

15:20.720 --> 15:24.420
<i>He </i>is<i> being kind of standoffish, isn't he?</i>

15:31.730 --> 15:33.760
Pass these out, will you?

15:33.760 --> 15:34.820
Sure.

15:34.820 --> 15:37.130
I don't feel like doing 
anything when it rains.

15:37.130 --> 15:38.830
What, you think you're 
a king or something?

15:38.830 --> 15:40.760
You two have a fight or something?

15:40.410 --> 15:41.210
<b>Japanese History</b>

15:41.210 --> 15:43.290
Wha... What gave you that idea?!

15:43.290 --> 15:44.920
Call it a hunch.

15:56.490 --> 16:00.430
Listen. This is about a friend. Not me.

16:00.430 --> 16:02.120
Huh? Okay...?

16:02.120 --> 16:03.420
<i>She's so obvious!</i>

16:03.420 --> 16:04.770
Her and this classmate?

16:04.770 --> 16:09.750
Things got awkward between them because 
they both said something without meaning it.

16:09.750 --> 16:14.320
Uh-huh. They may not have meant it, 
but did it upset the other person?

16:15.660 --> 16:18.570
<i>I don't know about that...</i>

16:18.570 --> 16:21.810
<i>I only said anything because Shima-kun 
skipped school like it was nothing!</i>

16:21.810 --> 16:23.740
<i>It sucks.</i>

16:23.740 --> 16:26.670
<i>Yeah! I was coming from a place of concern!</i>

16:26.670 --> 16:30.870
No, I think she was just 
worried about her friend!

16:30.870 --> 16:32.170
That so?

16:33.000 --> 16:37.320
Then maybe there's no need to 
bring it back up and apologize.

16:37.320 --> 16:40.640
If she said what she wanted to say, 
she should stick to her guns.

16:41.110 --> 16:43.650
What she wanted to say...?

16:44.710 --> 16:47.600
Huh? Hmm? Uh...

16:47.600 --> 16:48.900
What she wanted to say?

16:48.900 --> 16:51.600
<i>Look at the wheels turn.</i>

16:51.600 --> 16:54.990
<i>You've got the advantage 
of being class officers with him.</i>

16:54.990 --> 16:57.410
<i>Figure this out yourself.</i>

16:57.410 --> 16:59.750
<i>Did I say what I wanted to say?</i>

17:01.060 --> 17:03.740
What are you talking about?

17:03.740 --> 17:05.530
Nothing!

17:06.980 --> 17:08.250
Want a snack?

17:08.250 --> 17:10.650
You've got the good stuff, Makocchan.

17:10.650 --> 17:12.320
Croquettes from the school store?

17:26.460 --> 17:30.660
<i>It's true that I was worried and that 
I thought it wasn't the right thing to do.</i>

17:31.520 --> 17:35.060
<i>But was that what I wanted to say?</i>

17:35.060 --> 17:37.280
<i>Doesn't feel like it, for some reason.</i>

17:40.330 --> 17:45.270
<i>What was the first thought 
that sprang into my mind?</i>

17:56.050 --> 17:57.870
Sh... Shima-kun!

17:59.630 --> 18:01.430
Do you have a moment to talk?

18:14.990 --> 18:18.030
Hey, is this about yesterday?

18:18.780 --> 18:24.610
I'm sorry if I came off too harsh. 
I didn't mean to.

18:25.640 --> 18:28.990
I have some things to do 
at home today. We good?

18:28.990 --> 18:29.980
Got it.

18:29.980 --> 18:32.210
Then let me just say one thing.

18:33.960 --> 18:35.200
About yesterday...

18:35.890 --> 18:40.230
I'm sorry for getting on your case 
about exam season and stuff.

18:42.080 --> 18:44.220
I was saying things that 
made me sound justified,

18:45.150 --> 18:46.520
but the truth is...

18:50.110 --> 18:53.570
I want you to come to school 
because it's boring without you around.

18:53.570 --> 18:55.480
That's what I really wanted to say.

19:01.150 --> 19:03.010
Th... That's all!

19:03.010 --> 19:04.330
See you!

19:09.730 --> 19:10.670
Ah.

19:18.390 --> 19:22.890
My family is pretty uninvolved right now.

19:29.130 --> 19:31.710
We often don't even eat dinner together.

19:32.150 --> 19:35.980
And I'll often stay the night 
with a friend from my acting days.

19:36.530 --> 19:39.990
The third year of middle school, 
I'd stay out late due to cram school.

19:40.350 --> 19:41.760
What I'm saying is...

19:41.760 --> 19:46.990
I'm probably not as much of a mess 
as you're worried I am.

19:47.630 --> 19:49.840
I do skip here and there, though.

19:52.760 --> 19:54.340
Is that so?

19:54.340 --> 19:58.000
Ugh... My point is...

19:58.870 --> 20:03.260
I wasn't mad because I thought 
you were bugging me.

20:04.120 --> 20:09.130
I just hated the idea that you took 
those rumors about me seriously.

20:09.130 --> 20:12.470
Oh, I didn't! I just happened to hear it...

20:12.470 --> 20:14.770
It's fine. I get it.

20:15.850 --> 20:19.030
I'm used to people making up 
wild stories about me,

20:19.910 --> 20:21.740
but Mitsumi-chan...

20:21.740 --> 20:23.930
I don't want <i>you</i> to believe them!

20:23.930 --> 20:25.530
Don't even listen to them.

20:27.910 --> 20:29.750
Okay! I won't listen!

20:31.700 --> 20:34.670
I see. So it was that, huh?

20:35.240 --> 20:37.140
Sorry. That was insensitive of me.

20:40.610 --> 20:43.490
Huh? What? Did I say something funny?

20:44.300 --> 20:46.260
Nah, sorry. It's just...

20:50.660 --> 20:54.670
I haven't made up with someone 
so dramatically since grade school!

20:55.610 --> 20:57.430
What? Really?!

20:57.430 --> 21:00.790
Man, this is so funny. I can't stop laughing.

21:01.540 --> 21:03.030
What the heck?

21:03.030 --> 21:05.450
What's wrong with it every now and then?!

21:06.600 --> 21:10.030
Yeah, nothing wrong with it now and then.

21:11.380 --> 21:15.230
<i>Ugh, what is this feeling? 
Why do I feel so vulnerable?</i>

21:15.750 --> 21:19.250
<i>All I want to do is run away 
from here at full speed!</i>

21:19.250 --> 21:22.760
I'd keep worrying about 
the right things to say,

21:22.760 --> 21:24.540
keep wanting to
run away mid-sentence...

21:26.730 --> 21:28.890
Man, but you know what?

21:29.440 --> 21:35.520
I think this is the first time I've 
ever been real friends with a girl.

21:45.680 --> 21:46.700
<i>Huh?</i>

21:47.080 --> 21:48.820
<i>Why does it feel so stuffy?</i>

21:49.570 --> 21:53.200
<i>Today's forecast said the maximum 
temperature would only be 20C.</i>

21:53.980 --> 21:56.210
<i>Hello? What's up, Mitsumi-chan?</i>

21:56.210 --> 21:59.460
I think you can feel that way 
about a friend, too!

21:59.460 --> 22:02.510
<i>Huh? Wait, what? What are you talking about?</i>

22:05.290 --> 22:08.250
<i>Summer is almost upon us.</i>
